          "guid": "ms8o5q0pr4x5ohmd",
          "message": {
            "text": "draggable=\"false\" on the note-artifact image is the fix for the inverse of the drag-handle bug: omitting the attribute left native image drag on, competing with the drag-to-mark-a-region gesture.\n\nThe old draggable={false} rendered nothing at all — kerf omits a false boolean — and omission selects auto, which for an <img> means draggable. Confirmed in real Chromium: an <img> with no draggable attribute reads back el.draggable === true, while draggable=\"false\" reads false.\n\nThat matters specifically here because this image is the drag surface for marking a region (the title says so, and the sibling .ai-note-artifact-region-overlay is what the drag paints into). With native drag live, a press-and-move on the image could start a browser image-drag instead of the region gesture. The same one-word fix applies to the plugin-rendered SVG artifact above and to the shared lightbox image in src/client/lightbox.tsx — all three are drawn on or dragged over, and none of them should be natively draggable.\n\nSee also src/client/annotations/render.tsx, which carries the opposite half of this change (the handle that should be draggable and was not).\n",
            "markdown": "`draggable=\"false\"` on the note-artifact image is the fix for the inverse of the drag-handle bug: omitting the attribute left native image drag *on*, competing with the drag-to-mark-a-region gesture.\n\nThe old `draggable={false}` rendered nothing at all — kerf omits a false boolean — and omission selects `auto`, which for an `<img>` means draggable. Confirmed in real Chromium: an `<img>` with no `draggable` attribute reads back `el.draggable === true`, while `draggable=\"false\"` reads `false`.\n\nThat matters specifically here because this image is the drag surface for marking a region (the `title` says so, and the sibling `.ai-note-artifact-region-overlay` is what the drag paints into). With native drag live, a press-and-move on the image could start a browser image-drag instead of the region gesture. The same one-word fix applies to the plugin-rendered SVG artifact above and to the shared lightbox image in `src/client/lightbox.tsx` — all three are drawn on or dragged over, and none of them should be natively draggable.\n\nSee also `src/client/annotations/render.tsx`, which carries the opposite half of this change (the handle that *should* be draggable and was not).\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/components/diffView.tsx"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 465,
                  "endLine": 465,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "                      <img className=\"ai-note-artifact-img\" loading=\"lazy\" alt={a.uri} draggable=\"false\""
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
